  "question": {
    "text": "Three identical bars A, B and C are made of different magnetic materials. When kept in a uniform magnetic field, the field lines around them look as follows:\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/pcHay_y5s0hrmspzNqT80hWCImOw1TtMe8c0KyLn4-c.original.fullsize.png\"><br><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/juddoQN0CaReHXnbX_qVdH3RxxAbbBL73d5IEmj_5gM.original.fullsize.png\"><br><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/JZCr13N1kOgwZupx0lcebpkKMNjjQV6mz_qqA9SgSHE.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nMake the correspondence of these bars with their material being diamagnetic ( $\\mathrm{D})$, ferromagnetic (F) and paramagnetic $(\\mathrm{P})$ :",
    "image": null
  },
